A||N||3||Capt Fiero||Cruise Control||||1||
Z||000000||Capt Fiero||02-22-2000||12:41 PM||||Is my cruise broke or is that what it is supose to do.  I was on a long desert HWY over the weekend, setting up a Fiero Fest in Washington State.  This hwy is 200miles of flat straight smooth road, nothing around, I wanted to set the cruise at about 100mph the most the car would let me is 85mph. Is there some way to adjust it. It is kinda weird the car's cruise will accl all the way to 85 but them just stops and sits there. Broke or just set that way.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Oreif||02-22-2000||01:49 PM||||The vehicle speed sensor limits the cruise control to 85mph. I don't know if this is true for the GT's with the 120mph speedo. I would assume so since the VSS is the same part #. If all else fails try the Texas Cruise Control. (Brick on gas pedal  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> )||||reg||1
Z||000002||Capt Fiero||02-22-2000||02:10 PM||||Hmm, my car is an 85 GT that came stock with the 85mph speedo and the 125c transaxle.  I have replaced the speedo with the 120mph cluster (180kph here in Canada) I have replaced the VSS with a stock replacment. I could not believe how bad the gear was worn. I guess after 240,000 miles on the factory 125c tranny I did pretty well, and yes that is not a typo the stock auto trans is still holding after 240,000 miles. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||02-22-2000||07:19 PM||||The same VSS units are used for all speedometers. The exact VSS hardware used is tranny specific.<P>Niether the VSS nor the Speedo could be the limit as the ECM must be fed pulses as well. The ECM would be very unhappy if the pulses stoped at 85mph. The speedo is where the divider that reduces the 4000ppm to 2000ppm is. ((All Fiero ECM's run on 2000ppm. The speedo uses 4000ppm.))<P>Only in the 87 and up 4 cyl cars could the ECM be the limiter. On the DIS cars the cruise unit is coded and wired into the ECM main logic. Prior to that it is a sub board/module that recieves the same 2000ppm as the ECM does. I think the sub module uses a chip from national semiconductor. (It's been awhile since I looked it up.) I believe that chip is hard coded to 85.||||reg||1
